      "content": "what i mean by \"letting go\" is... everything is just empty now. i don't have my community, my work, my identity. it's like the soul of me was tied to that digital life and since that's gone, there isn't really a \"me\" left to save. it feels like it would just be more logical to finish what already happened. does that even make sense? like, why bother staying when the person i was is already dead?",
